  "details": "(this bug was reported by @ArcWAG on twitter, I'm translating it on their behalf)\n\nSample avatar: https://vrchat.com/home/avatar/avtr_17a01d30-a2fb-4bf8-baf1-9c82e12a8529\n\nWhen you select \"cube reset\" from the menu, the size of the cube in front of you should reset. However, on open beta, this gimmick does not work properly.\n\n# Repro steps\n\nPlace the following objects at the root of the avatar.\n\nObject A (contains an animation to set object B's scale to 1)\n\n -> Object B (contains an animation to increase its own scale)\n\n    -> Cube\n\n- Object A: Contains an animator. Plays an animation to set object B's scale to 1\n\n- Object B contains an animator. Increases its own scale\n\n- Cube: Unity's default cube (for debugging)\n\nIn the FX layer, set up animations to activate just one of either A or B's animator, and turn the other off, and set up a menu to switch between these.\n\nExpected behavior:\n\nWhen you disable A's animator and enable B's, the cube gets larger. Then, if you disable B's animator and enable A's animator, the cube's side returns to normal.\n\nOpen beta:\n\nWhen you disable A and enable B, the cube gets larger. Then, when you disable B and enable A, the cube's size remains large.",
